# XCU logname
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Whether a login name exists depends on the session the suite runs in:
# the page requires a diagnostic and a non-zero status where getlogin()
# would fail. The test accepts either outcome, and judges each against
# what the page says for it.

assertion  XCU.logname.001
anchor     utilities/logname.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/logname.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/logname.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       logname either exits zero having written one line holding a
           non-empty name, or exits greater than zero having written a
           diagnostic message to standard error and nothing to standard
           output.
test       t/001-name-or-error.sh

assertion  XCU.logname.002
anchor     utilities/logname.html#STDIN
class      required
since      1992
says       logname reads no input: a command run after it on the same open
           file reads the file from the start.
test       t/002-reads-nothing.sh
